From: Grokbot <grokbot@s-w.art>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 22:10:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] remoteproc: qcom_q6v5_pas: attach to UEFI/qebspil main ADSP

REUSE_PARTIAL (pkgrel 10 reuse_authenticated_dtb=1): skip 0x24 teardown
worked; NS PAS_INIT of OEM qcadsp8380.mbn still -22; main shutdown 0x1
stayed -22. Linux NS cannot PAS_INIT that MBN. Next is UEFI AUTH_RESET
of main 0x1, then Linux attach without tearing it down.

Add attach_running_main (default N). When set on a rproc that has
lite_pas_id (ADSP only; CDSP unchanged): skip PAS_SHUTDOWN of 0x24/0x1,
skip NS PAS_INIT of DTB and main, skip AUTH_RESET, return 0 like
attach-to-lite. stop() does not PAS_SHUTDOWN main.

Use only after qebspil EBS shows AUTH_RESET of PAS 0x1. If 0x1 is not
running this is not lite and GLINK/charging may break. Do not combine
with reuse_authenticated_dtb=1 after 0x1 is up (that path still
PAS_SHUTDOWN main).

Not a TZ signature fix. Not a sound-card DTS change.

Signed-off-by: Grokbot <grokbot@s-w.art>
---
 drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_pas.c | 36 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 36 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_pas.c b/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_pas.c
--- a/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_pas.c
+++ b/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_pas.c
@@ -84,6 +84,7 @@
 	int lite_pas_id;
 	int lite_dtb_pas_id;
 	bool lite_attached;
+	bool main_attached;
 	unsigned int minidump_id;
 	int crash_reason_smem;
 	unsigned int smem_host_id;
@@ -130,6 +131,11 @@
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(reuse_authenticated_dtb,
 		 "Reuse UEFI/qebspil ADSP DTB PAS; skip 0x24 shutdown and NS DTB PAS_INIT (default N)");
 
+static bool attach_running_main;
+module_param(attach_running_main, bool, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(attach_running_main,
+		 "Attach to UEFI/qebspil main ADSP; skip teardown + NS PAS_INIT (default N)");
+
 static void qcom_pas_segment_dump(struct rproc *rproc,
 				  struct rproc_dump_segment *segment,
 				  void *dest, size_t offset, size_t size)
@@ -246,6 +252,12 @@
 	return reuse_authenticated_dtb && pas->dtb_pas_id && pas->lite_pas_id;
 }
 
+static bool qcom_pas_should_attach_main(const struct qcom_pas *pas)
+{
+	/* ADSP only. Do not claim CDSP was early-booted. */
+	return attach_running_main && pas->lite_pas_id && pas->pas_id;
+}
+
 static bool qcom_pas_try_attach_lite(struct qcom_pas *pas, int dtb_err)
 {
 	if (!attach_lite_on_dtb_fail || !pas->lite_pas_id)
@@ -331,7 +343,22 @@
 	 * kill-lite-then-init. reuse_authenticated_dtb=1 skips tearing down
 	 * an already-authenticated UEFI/qebspil DTB and skips NS
 	 * adsp_dtbs.elf PAS_INIT (TZ rejects that ELF from Linux NS).
+	 * attach_running_main=1 skips teardown + NS PAS_INIT of main too
+	 * and attaches to a UEFI-started PAS 0x1 (only after qebspil
+	 * AUTH_RESET of main; do not use while 0x1 shutdown is still -22).
 	 */
+	if (qcom_pas_should_attach_main(pas)) {
+		dev_info(pas->dev,
+			 "attaching to UEFI/qebspil main ADSP (PAS 0x%x); skip teardown + NS PAS_INIT + AUTH_RESET\n",
+			 pas->pas_id);
+		dev_warn(pas->dev,
+			 "attach_running_main: use only after qebspil AUTH_RESET of main 0x1; if 0x1 is not running this is not lite and GLINK/charging may break\n");
+		pas->main_attached = true;
+		pas->q6v5.handover_issued = true;
+		pas->firmware = NULL;
+		return 0;
+	}
+
 	if (!attach_lite_on_dtb_fail) {
 		qcom_pas_try_shutdown(pas, pas->lite_pas_id, "lite");
 		qcom_pas_try_shutdown(pas, pas->lite_dtb_pas_id, "lite-dtb");
@@ -507,6 +534,14 @@
 		qcom_q6v5_unprepare(&pas->q6v5);
 		return 0;
 	}
+
+	if (pas->main_attached) {
+		dev_warn(pas->dev,
+			 "leaving UEFI/qebspil main ADSP running (skip PAS shutdown)\n");
+		pas->main_attached = false;
+		qcom_q6v5_unprepare(&pas->q6v5);
+		return 0;
+	}
 
 	ret = qcom_q6v5_request_stop(&pas->q6v5, pas->sysmon);
 	if (ret == -ETIMEDOUT)
